  "body": "In the editor, when viewing a series of shots of the same subject, it can sometimes be difficult to tell which thumbnail corresponds to the image currently displayed when you’ve clicked on a different thumbnail for any reason. Yes we can look at the name of the picture at the first line or consider it is always in the middle. \nIn the settings, the “Highlight Thumbnail” option is redundant with highlight of the background of the thumbnail corresponding to the selected thumbnail.\nThis option could instead be dedicated to the image currently displayed for editing.\n\n<img width=\"1543\" height=\"1084\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb7b24cb-93c8-4b46-b3c5-81d725a03605\" />",
